{
 "name": "mount_cleveland",
 "description": "Mount Cleveland (Glacier National Park's highest peak) as a steep dark-rock tower under ice and snow: lit rock #7a6a58 left face with strata lines, two red-argillite bands, shadowed right face #6b5b4b/#5a4b3d, snow cap and snow ledges #f7fbff / ice streaks #dfe7ee / shadow snow #c9d8e4. No flag. Anchor bottom-centre; summit exactly at (0,-900). Left face (the climb) is a straight edge from (-450,0) to (0,-900); right face a straight edge from (0,-900) to (550,0) (tiny notches only). Low shoulders spread to x -650 / +700 below y -150. x -650..700, y -900..0.",
